<article class="env-lemma" id="02MV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02MV">Lemma <span data-tag="02MV">12.11.2</span>.</a> Let $F : \mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{B}$ be an exact functor between abelian categories. Then $F$ induces a homomorphism of $K$-groups $K_0(F) : K_0(\mathcal{A}) \to K_0(\mathcal{B})$ by simply setting $K_0(F)([A]) = [F(A)]$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
